{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records as Segment-spec track calls to Segment, RudderStack or Customer.io Data Pipelines."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Segment, RudderStack and Customer.io Data Pipelines each take the same batch call of the Segment"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spec, at endpoints of their own. One encoder, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", writes it, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"factory for each fills in the endpoint and how the key travels:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" posts to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/v1\/batch"},{"text":" of the workspace’s region (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentRegion","type":"reference"},{"text":"), with the write key as HTTP Basic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"authentication’s user name and an empty password.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" posts to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"code":"\/v1\/batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" of your data plane URL, with the write key the same way."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":" posts to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Pipelines API’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/v1\/batch"},{"type":"text","text":" in the workspace’s region ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIORegion"},{"type":"text","text":"), with the key as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bearer token and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"X-Strict-Mode: 1"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each splits a batch to the spec’s limits ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":"): 2,500 calls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and 500 KB a request, and under 32 KB a call, which all three accept. A batch with no record the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. Each retries no response, a 5xx, 408"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaves this module out; import it on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The key goes in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Authorization"},{"type":"text","text":" header field, never in the body. It is a public client key:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Segment’s and RudderStack’s write keys, and Customer.io’s public keys ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pk_…"},{"type":"text","text":"), ship in their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vendors’ own app and web libraries, and they let a client send data to the source and read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io’s private keys ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sk_…"},{"type":"text","text":") reach every Customer.io API, deleting people included, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the factory throws "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError\/privateKey"},{"type":"text","text":" for one. Each factory throws for an empty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/RudderStackSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":"), RudderStack’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for a data plane URL that isn’t a plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https"},{"type":"text","text":" URL, and Customer.io’s for a public key of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other region."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A region has no default. Segment and Customer.io keep a workspace’s data in the US or the EU, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events posted to the other region’s endpoint don’t reach it, so you pick the region on purpose.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record becomes a track call of an anonymous user. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s session,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the sessions enricher; a record with no session is sent under its own record identifier. No","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call or traits are sent. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s identifier, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a redelivered record keeps, and its ","type":"text"},{"code":"timestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the record’s timestamp in ISO 8601 with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent. The standard context","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"goes in the spec’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"context","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" fields (","type":"text"},{"code":"app","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"device","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"locale","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"network","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"os","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"device.id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"advertisingId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call’s "},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which Segment takes in place of the request’s address, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it records none. RudderStack fills in a "},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from the request unless the call has one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"even beside "},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and passes it on to its destinations, so RudderStack’s calls also carry"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Customer.io’s references don’t say whether "},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" takes the place"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the address it reads from an HTTP request, so it may still record the request’s."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each endpoint counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymousId"},{"type":"text","text":", so each session is one user in its reports, and so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is each record sent without a session. On a plan billed by monthly tracked users, each counts as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. A record a store recovers after a relaunch has no session, so it goes out under its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier. Segment deduplicates calls by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageId"},{"type":"text","text":", which the record keeps, and drops most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"duplicates within about 24 hours, not all, so one it stored before the app ended is most likely"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not stored again. RudderStack’s and Customer.io’s API references don’t say whether they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deduplicate, so such a record may be stored twice there."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the encoder can’t write is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one named as one of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Customer.io’s semantic events, which delete or suppress people and devices (","type":"text"},{"code":"User Deleted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"User Suppressed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Device Deleted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the rest), one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one holding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form, and one too large for a call. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination reports each as ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose reason is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError","type":"reference"},{"text":", and the encoder logs a notice for each semantic event name in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plan when the destination is made.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Segment answers 200 for every request but one too large or not JSON, so a wrong region, a write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key of no source, or a batch of more calls than it takes may be answered 200 with nothing stored."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Check the source’s debugger after setting the destination up. RudderStack answers a wrong write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key with 401, and Customer.io, in strict mode, with 401 too, so the destination reports those. In"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"strict mode Customer.io refuses a whole batch for one bad call, so the encoder leaves out each call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io documents refusing; a 400 for anything else drops the whole request."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to PostHog, Amplitude or Mixpanel, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AmplitudeEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import HTTPDestinations","import SegmentSpecEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let segment = try HTTPDestination.segment(","    writeKey: writeKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the workspace is","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: segment)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what each endpoint receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-Segment","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentRegion","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSetupError"],"title":"Sending to Segment"},{"anchor":"Sending-to-RudderStack","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/RudderStackSetupError"],"title":"Sending to RudderStack"},{"anchor":"Sending-to-Customerio-Data-Pipelines","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIORegion","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError"],"title":"Sending to Customer.io Data Pipelines"},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"],"title":"Encoding batches"},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError"],"title":"Records left out"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","externalID":"SegmentSpecEncoding","symbolKind":"module","title":"SegmentSpecEncoding","modules":[{"name":"SegmentSpecEncoding"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)":{"conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transport"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSessionTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encoding"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends batches to the RudderStack source of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"writeKey"},{"type":"text","text":", through the data"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plane at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dataPlane"},{"type":"text","text":", with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession.shared"},{"type":"text","text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"waits of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/rudderstack(writekey:dataplane:plan:backoff:clock:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rudderStack","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"writeKey","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dataPlane","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials3URLV","text":"URL","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"plan","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","text":"TrackingPlan","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"backoff","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clock","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","text":"Clock","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding21RudderStackSetupErrorO","text":"RudderStackSetupError","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations19URLSessionTransportV","text":"URLSessionTransport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/SegmentSetupError":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"SegmentSetupError","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSetupError","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentSetupError","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"couldn’t make a destination."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentSetupError","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/segmentsetuperror"},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/RudderStackSetupError":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/RudderStackSetupError","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/rudderstacksetuperror","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RudderStackSetupError","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"couldn’t make a destination.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RudderStackSetupError","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"RudderStackSetupError"},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"customerIO"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"apiKey"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"region"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding16CustomerIORegionO","text":"CustomerIORegion"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","text":"TrackingPlan"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"backoff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","text":"ExponentialBackoff"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clock"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","text":"Clock"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":">) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding20CustomerIOSetupErrorO","text":"CustomerIOSetupError"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","text":"HTTPDestination"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations19URLSessionTransportV","text":"URLSessionTransport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"conformance":{"constraints":[{"code":"Transport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSessionTransport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text